# Example ufw rules for fs-dev (Debian)
#
# Review interface names (e.g. eth0, enp0s3, tailscale0) before applying.
#
#   sudo ufw default deny incoming
#   sudo ufw default allow outgoing
#
# SSH (22) — restrict to your LAN if desired:
#   sudo ufw allow in on eth0 from 192.168.4.0/24 to any port 22 proto tcp
#   sudo ufw allow OpenSSH
#
# HTTPS (443) on LAN primary NIC:
#   sudo ufw allow in on eth0 from 192.168.4.0/24 to any port 443 proto tcp
#
# HTTPS via Tailscale (tailnet); interface is usually tailscale0:
#   sudo ufw allow in on tailscale0 to any port 443 proto tcp
#
# Explicitly do NOT expose the control API on the LAN:
#   sudo ufw deny in on eth0 to any port 8000 proto tcp
#
#   sudo ufw enable
#   sudo ufw status verbose
#
# Port 8000 must remain loopback-only (systemd binds 127.0.0.1). Caddy terminates TLS on 443.
